course: dictionary
lesson: 3226
title: Enthusiasm: keen and eager
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Enthusiasm is a strong feeling of excitement and keen interest in something, so much that you really want to do it. When you meet it in a text, look at the words around it. Teachers praise pupils who show enthusiasm for learning, and a coach likes players who train with enthusiasm.
explain: Try the swap check. Put «keen interest» in place of enthusiasm: «Many musicians today are glad of the keen interest» still makes sense, so enthusiasm must mean something close to that. Being full of enthusiasm means you are eager and keen, not bored or half-hearted.
explain: Enthusiasm can also be a countable noun, meaning a hobby or interest that you love. «Dinosaurs are his great enthusiasm» tells you that dinosaurs are the hobby he loves most. Look for the word "his" or "her" before it, and you will often find a hobby.
fact: Enthusiasm means a strong feeling of excitement and keen interest in something.
fact: Enthusiasm is usually uncountable: you show enthusiasm, or you have enthusiasm for something.
fact: An enthusiasm (countable) is a hobby or interest that you love, as in «Dinosaurs are his great enthusiasm.»
fact: Useful phrases: «with enthusiasm», «full of enthusiasm», «show enthusiasm», «lose your enthusiasm», «enthusiasm for».
fact: In the clapping example, «many musicians today are glad of the enthusiasm» shows that musicians like it when audiences are excited.
exercise: The coach smiled and said, «Your enthusiasm is brilliant!» What does enthusiasm mean here? | *Strong excitement and keen interest | Tiredness after a long run | A kind of sports shoe | Being cross with the team
exercise: «Dinosaurs are his great enthusiasm.» What does enthusiasm mean here? | A place he likes to visit | A kind of fossil | *A hobby he loves | A dislike of school
exercise: Mia started her project full of enthusiasm, but by Friday she had lost it. What had she lost? | Her voice | Her lunch box | Her pencil case | *Her excitement and keen interest
test: Ravi worked on his model with real enthusiasm and never stopped until it was finished. Which word is closest in meaning to enthusiasm? | Anger | Boredom | Sleepiness | *Eagerness
test: «She spoke about her enthusiasm for maths.» Which swap keeps the sentence sensible? | She spoke about her boredom with maths | *She spoke about her keen interest in maths | She spoke about her fear of maths | She spoke about her cold feet in maths
exam: Which sentence uses enthusiasm to mean a hobby you love? | The class showed great enthusiasm during the quiz | Enthusiasm makes the day longer | He lost his enthusiasm at lunch | *Painting seascapes is her great enthusiasm
